## Generic Rules (Reusable)

### Code Quality (`generic/code-quality/`)

| File                     | Description                                | Tokens | Priority |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ | ------ | -------- |
| `clean-code.mdx`         | Clean code principles, SOLID, DRY          | 400    | High     |
| `typescript.mdx`         | TypeScript strict mode, patterns           | 350    | High     |
| `naming-conventions.mdx` | Naming guidelines for variables, functions | 200    | Medium   |

**Use When:** Writing any code, code review, refactoring

**Key Principles:**

- Max 30 lines per function
- Max 5 parameters per function
- Use strict types, avoid `any`
- Explicit constants, no magic numbers
- Long, readable variable names

### Error Handling (`generic/error-handling/`)

| File                 | Description                       | Tokens | Priority |
| -------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------ | -------- |
| `error-handling.mdx` | Error patterns, logging, recovery | 300    | High     |

**Use When:** Implementing error handling, debugging

**Patterns:**

- Try-catch with specific error types
- User-friendly error messages
- Graceful degradation
- Error logging and monitoring

